## Stack (mandatory)
- React Native + Expo + TypeScript strict · Expo Router
- **React Native Reusables** (UI primitives — incremental CLI add)
- **NativeWind v4** (styling + WMS tokens) · TanStack Query · React Hook Form + Zod
- AsyncStorage (temporary POC persistence only) · Expo Image/Document Picker

## Architecture (non-negotiable)
`Screen -> feature hook/use-case -> repository interface -> mock repository now / API repository later`
- No direct JSON fixture imports from screens; no direct storage/API calls from UI.
- Mock data behind typed repository/service interfaces; business logic outside presentational components.
- Avoid `any`; explicit domain types. Reusable UI + centralized tokens.
- **Backend-adaptable (mandatory):** every repository method = a future REST endpoint (GET/POST/PUT/DELETE) on a NestJS/FastAPI backend. JSON DTOs, stable IDs, ISO-8601 dates, EUR minor units, idempotency keys on payment/registration. Swap point = `src/data/providers/repositories.ts`. See `DELIVERY_PLAN_COMO2027.md` §6.6.

## Masters rules engine (the core differentiator)
- Rules are **configuration**, versioned + effective-dated + audited. Age reference date default **31 Dec 2027**. No silent reclassification (RUL series).
- Patterns: individual bands, **youngest-member**, **crew-average (excl. coxswain)**, **relay-aggregate**, proficiency grade, judo multi-dimension, golf handicap, para class (restricted).
- Engine = pure functions in `src/features/rules/*`, consumed via a `useRules` hook + `RulesRepository` interface. Every rule effect must be **visible on screen** (recalc, warning, impact analysis).

## POC boundaries (D5)
- No real backend, OTP provider, payment gateway, malware scanner, or scoring engine unless explicitly requested — mock behind interfaces.
- Deterministic demo data: **Daniel Harper, Marco Rossi**, Como Lake 2027 (swimming/basketball/rowing/tennis). Seed = `DELIVERY_PLAN_COMO2027.md` §6.3.
- Sensitive data (medical/para/ID) modelled **restricted** from day one.

## Screens (Como two-portal — replaces the old A01–A18 flow)
- **Participant Portal:** claim pre-reg → profile & consent → dynamic sport/event entry (live rule check) → evidence → partner/team roster → change-impact → checkout → waitlist offer → registration dashboard → digital accreditation → results.
- **Admin OC Command Centre:** ops/SLA dashboard, exception queue (dual approval), sport rules configurator, finance reconciliation (P0); accreditation desk + comms center (P1).
- Full screen map: `BUSINESS_OVERVIEW_COMO2027.md` §7. Build per `DELIVERY_PLAN_COMO2027.md` workstreams — do not build everything at once.

## Language & accessibility (mandatory, not P1-only)
- **English + Italian** on the demo path from P0 (RFP PLT-02). **WCAG 2.2 AA** (older users) — critical registration-path barriers are release blockers (ACS series).

## Platform strategy: hybrid responsive, Expo Web first
- One React Native codebase — no separate React/Vite app. Left-nav portal on desktop + usable mobile views from day one (D2).
- Develop/review primarily on **Expo Web**; validate Android/iOS after each major batch. No DOM-only APIs in screens.

## Progress and revisions (mandatory)
- **Start each session:** read `context_docs/docs/START_HERE.md` + `PROGRESS_COMO2027.md` + `REVISIONS.md`.
- **End each session:** update `PROGRESS_COMO2027.md`; log plan/stack changes in `REVISIONS.md` (new `REV-###`) before marking work done.

## Definition of done (per screen)
- Matches design system + portal shell · correct navigation · canonical seed data via repositories
- Primary interaction + relevant states (loading/empty/error/pending/waitlisted/approved/etc.)
- Responsive (desktop + mobile) · EN+IT on demo path · rule effects visible · no direct JSON import · strict TypeScript
